WEBVTT

00:43.043 --> 00:46.672
CHAPTER 34:
I'M THEIR HOMEROOM TEACHER

00:47.757 --> 00:50.259
So the US, huh? I bet you're thrilled.

00:50.342 --> 00:54.555
Then again, a lot of colleges
wanted you to join them, right?

00:54.638 --> 00:59.351
Then, are you going somewhere
like Harvard or MIT to conduct research

00:59.435 --> 01:01.604
or are you going there to teach?

01:04.648 --> 01:06.942
How long would you be away?

01:07.026 --> 01:08.611
A semester? A year?

01:09.487 --> 01:11.238
I guess what I'm asking…

01:11.822 --> 01:12.948
What I want to know is…

01:15.367 --> 01:17.620
If you're going away for a long time,

01:18.662 --> 01:22.666
does that mean
I won't see you in my senior year?

01:30.966 --> 01:32.843
It's late. Go home.

01:37.014 --> 01:38.098
Get home safely, Eui-ju.

01:48.275 --> 01:50.486
So, when are you leaving?

01:59.119 --> 02:00.996
About that proposal
from your friend Deul-i.

02:01.664 --> 02:02.790
What do you think?

02:05.084 --> 02:07.169
So seize this opportunity
and go to the US.

02:07.253 --> 02:08.420
Go do the research you want to do.

02:14.927 --> 02:15.761
Still,

02:16.470 --> 02:18.556
does he have to go with her?

02:20.307 --> 02:21.308
So,

02:22.309 --> 02:24.186
is she his girlfriend after all?

02:27.398 --> 02:28.732
Well,

02:28.816 --> 02:31.777
he's a person just like the rest of us.
Of course, he's gonna date.

02:35.531 --> 02:37.449
They'll do research together

02:38.409 --> 02:39.952
in the US.

02:40.703 --> 02:41.829
Just the two of them.

02:43.998 --> 02:44.999
Good for them.

02:50.170 --> 02:51.255
Hang on.

02:51.338 --> 02:53.173
If I hadn't overheard them earlier,

02:53.257 --> 02:55.009
when was he planning on telling me?

02:56.218 --> 02:57.344
At the end of the year?

02:57.428 --> 02:59.722
Like, "Bye, kids. I'm off to the US."

03:04.768 --> 03:05.769
No.

03:07.146 --> 03:09.106
Why would he bother saying anything?

03:10.190 --> 03:13.485
It's his life after all.

03:15.029 --> 03:17.448
I'm just one of his students.

03:28.626 --> 03:30.628
EPISODE 11

03:34.757 --> 03:38.636
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

03:43.682 --> 03:45.225
Is everyone here except Ji-a and Jenny?

03:45.976 --> 03:47.561
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

03:47.645 --> 03:49.563
The career experience program signup
closes this week.

03:49.647 --> 03:51.440
Check the notice in our group chat.

03:52.483 --> 03:53.609
If you're interested,

03:53.692 --> 03:55.694
fill out an application
and give it to Ha-su.

03:56.362 --> 03:57.279
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

03:57.363 --> 03:59.573
-Collect them and bring them to me.
-Yes, sir.

04:01.116 --> 04:02.117
Dismissed.

04:02.201 --> 04:03.869
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

04:07.623 --> 04:10.167
Ji-a's absent again today.
What are you going to do?

04:10.250 --> 04:12.127
Won't he give you more demerits?

04:13.337 --> 04:14.880
Do you think something happened to her?

04:16.173 --> 04:17.007
Like what?

04:17.091 --> 04:18.801
I don't know.

04:33.399 --> 04:35.734
CLOUD YOUTH SHELTER

04:35.818 --> 04:36.902
Can I help you?

04:37.528 --> 04:38.445
Hello.

04:38.529 --> 04:41.949
I'm Yeo Eui-ju,
and I'm Ji-a's classmate at school.

04:42.032 --> 04:45.953
Ji-a didn't come to school today,
so I was wondering if she's okay.

04:46.036 --> 04:48.080
She's not here right now.

04:48.580 --> 04:49.999
I think she's at her part-time job.

04:52.209 --> 04:53.794
Do you know where she works?

04:54.420 --> 04:55.546
Where was it again?

04:56.922 --> 04:59.091
I believe it's a burger joint.

04:59.174 --> 05:01.093
The one at the intersection
by the Red Cross Hospital.

05:02.469 --> 05:03.387
I see.

05:04.054 --> 05:05.973
-Thank you.
-I should be thanking you

05:06.056 --> 05:07.349
for coming here to check on her.

05:07.975 --> 05:08.809
Bye.

05:16.567 --> 05:17.776
Mr. Ga.

05:19.653 --> 05:21.363
Ji-a isn't here right now.

05:21.447 --> 05:22.823
She's probably at her work.

05:24.158 --> 05:25.617
How come you're here?

05:27.119 --> 05:30.622
I saw her write this place
as her address last year.

05:32.666 --> 05:34.209
I'll go look for her. You can go home now.

05:36.879 --> 05:38.088
I don't want to.

05:39.089 --> 05:41.050
I'm fed up with cleaning
to offset my demerits.

05:41.133 --> 05:42.551
I must see her myself today.

05:45.387 --> 05:46.388
But…

05:54.521 --> 05:56.065
-Ji-a?
-Yes.

05:56.148 --> 05:57.232
She quit.

05:57.816 --> 05:59.526
What? When?

06:00.986 --> 06:01.820
Maybe two weeks ago.

06:01.904 --> 06:03.530
No, about three weeks ago.

06:04.490 --> 06:07.618
Then do you know where she is right now?

06:08.619 --> 06:09.536
Some barbecue place.

06:09.620 --> 06:11.872
She said they offered a better pay.

06:12.539 --> 06:14.124
-Do you know the name?
-No, I don't.

06:14.208 --> 06:15.751
I didn't ask, you see.

06:17.419 --> 06:19.463
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

06:25.677 --> 06:27.763
I'll go this way, you go that way.

06:27.846 --> 06:29.223
-Call me if you find her.
-Okay.

07:02.923 --> 07:03.757
What the…

07:05.801 --> 07:06.927
Jeez.

07:07.553 --> 07:08.595
What's wrong with them?

07:10.305 --> 07:11.306
Come with me.

07:12.891 --> 07:14.476
What do you think you're doing?

07:14.560 --> 07:15.561
Are you crazy?

07:15.644 --> 07:18.230
Hey, how can you just take drinks
from them like that?

07:18.313 --> 07:19.815
Do they know you're in high school?

07:20.774 --> 07:21.733
They tip me.

07:22.317 --> 07:23.443
Wouldn't you drink?

07:24.862 --> 07:26.321
Even so…

07:26.405 --> 07:28.073
Ji-a?

07:29.032 --> 07:29.908
-Ji-a.
-Is that you?

07:29.992 --> 07:31.285
It's her, all right.

07:33.537 --> 07:36.498
Today's the day we agreed on, no?

07:37.457 --> 07:39.585
I haven't been paid yet.

07:39.668 --> 07:40.961
-But next time--
-"Next time"?

07:42.379 --> 07:44.339
That's what you said last time.

07:45.299 --> 07:46.925
Do you think we're running a charity?

07:47.676 --> 07:51.180
We're not some philanthropists.
We have to make a living too, you know?

07:51.722 --> 07:53.182
I really don't have any money.

07:53.682 --> 07:56.393
Then do whatever it takes to get it.

07:56.476 --> 07:57.853
Plenty of places would hire you.

07:58.437 --> 08:00.272
Convenience stores, coffee shops,

08:00.355 --> 08:01.231
karaokes,

08:01.315 --> 08:03.066
bars.

08:04.401 --> 08:05.903
The way I see it,

08:06.653 --> 08:08.614
-you could go far--
-What are you doing?

08:08.697 --> 08:10.407
Stop it.

08:10.490 --> 08:11.408
Are you Ji-a's friend?

08:12.201 --> 08:13.452
Oh, a friend?

08:13.535 --> 08:16.538
We're not going to hurt her.
We're not bad guys.

08:16.622 --> 08:20.500
If you're that worried,
why don't you pay on her behalf?

08:21.335 --> 08:22.711
Do you have any money?

08:23.503 --> 08:24.755
-That's enough.
-So?

08:24.838 --> 08:26.131
You're scaring her.

08:26.215 --> 08:27.466
So then,

08:27.549 --> 08:29.468
how much can you give us today?

08:30.177 --> 08:31.762
I don't have any money.

08:31.845 --> 08:32.804
I haven't been paid.

08:33.847 --> 08:35.891
-You've got to be kidding me.
-What are you doing?

08:35.974 --> 08:37.142
-Let me go!
-Stop that!

08:37.684 --> 08:38.560
You shouldn't be…

08:38.644 --> 08:40.062
What the heck?

08:41.980 --> 08:42.898
-Oh, man.
-What the hell?

08:42.981 --> 08:44.233
What do you think you're doing?

08:44.942 --> 08:45.901
And who might you be?

08:45.984 --> 08:47.778
I'm their homeroom teacher.

08:50.072 --> 08:52.741
-You scared me.
-Oh, their teacher?

08:53.325 --> 08:57.246
This is actually better.
Perhaps you can repay us on her behalf.

08:57.329 --> 08:59.206
You gave her this bruise, didn't you?

09:00.165 --> 09:01.833
We don't know anything about that.

09:02.626 --> 09:03.460
Sir.

09:04.461 --> 09:07.589
She borrowed money from us, okay?

09:07.673 --> 09:10.467
I guess you don't teach students
to repay their debts.

09:10.968 --> 09:11.927
Looks like it.

09:15.597 --> 09:16.640
How much did she borrow?

09:16.723 --> 09:18.558
How much? Let's see…

09:19.226 --> 09:21.770
She borrowed 500,000 won.

09:21.853 --> 09:23.981
But with interest, it's two million won,

09:24.856 --> 09:25.691
sir.

09:27.651 --> 09:28.860
And that's all?

09:30.070 --> 09:30.904
Mr. Ga!

09:31.655 --> 09:32.781
Oh, sweet.

09:32.864 --> 09:35.325
Dang, you're pretty cool.

09:35.409 --> 09:36.535
So sick.

09:36.618 --> 09:39.204
In that case, here.

09:39.288 --> 09:42.416
Wire the money to the account
at the bottom there.

09:43.792 --> 09:45.085
I've transferred it.

09:45.168 --> 09:46.378
-Oh, now?
-Did it come through?

09:46.461 --> 09:47.921
-Yeah.
-So it did.

09:49.339 --> 09:51.341
Let's make video evidence of this.

09:53.969 --> 09:55.804
-On November 10th,
-Yeah.

09:56.430 --> 09:59.224
we received two million won
from Choi Ji-a.

09:59.308 --> 10:00.142
Indeed, we did.

10:00.225 --> 10:01.351
From now on,

10:01.935 --> 10:04.146
we'll never contact her again.

10:04.646 --> 10:06.273
-Is that okay?
-Are we done?

10:07.357 --> 10:09.067
Delete her phone number right now.

10:09.151 --> 10:11.028
-Let me look up Ji-a.
-Here.

10:11.111 --> 10:12.779
Number deleted.

10:12.863 --> 10:13.947
DELETE NUMBER

10:14.031 --> 10:15.532
-Okay?
-Satisfied?

10:15.615 --> 10:17.659
I don't want to see you ever again.

10:17.743 --> 10:19.578
-Yes, sir.
-You got it.

10:20.537 --> 10:23.790
-It really was an honor to meet you.
-Totally.

10:23.874 --> 10:25.208
-If you ever need money,
-Oh, right.

10:25.876 --> 10:26.877
call us here

10:27.502 --> 10:29.296
-Yes.
-at the number on this business card.

10:30.130 --> 10:31.840
-Call us any time.
-We'll give you a good deal.

10:32.466 --> 10:34.134
-Bye.
-Ji-a, we're off.

10:34.217 --> 10:35.052
Bye now.

10:43.310 --> 10:44.269
Mr. Ga.

10:45.979 --> 10:47.356
I'll pay you back no matter what.

10:47.856 --> 10:50.400
It might take a while,

10:50.484 --> 10:51.985
but I'll make sure to pay you back.

10:53.362 --> 10:54.196
There's no need.

10:54.821 --> 10:57.574
Just make sure you come to school
and try your hardest.

10:59.284 --> 11:01.495
-Still…
-If you really want to repay this debt,

11:02.371 --> 11:03.663
save it for later

11:04.664 --> 11:06.625
and pay it forward if some kid needs help.

11:12.506 --> 11:14.049
-What are you doing?
-Huh?

11:16.218 --> 11:17.219
Well…

11:17.302 --> 11:19.596
You never know.
I'm taking a photo for evidence.

11:21.223 --> 11:23.475
You just love capturing
every single moment, don't you?

11:24.601 --> 11:25.477
Let's go.

11:28.271 --> 11:29.815
-Get a move on.
-Okay.

11:35.570 --> 11:38.448
Why didn't you report it?

11:39.616 --> 11:42.577
Another kid at the shelter
went through a similar situation.

11:43.787 --> 11:46.581
She got harassed
to repay the loan with steep interest.

11:47.791 --> 11:49.584
They did report the loan sharks,

11:49.668 --> 11:52.003
but they came to the shelter
and caused trouble.

11:53.797 --> 11:55.632
That kid had to leave the shelter

11:55.715 --> 11:57.551
for putting the other kids at risk.

12:00.262 --> 12:01.388
I see.

12:02.556 --> 12:05.600
Does this mean you can cut back
on your part-time jobs?

12:08.145 --> 12:08.979
No.

12:09.604 --> 12:10.605
I need to earn more.

12:11.815 --> 12:14.067
I have to leave the shelter next year.

12:14.693 --> 12:15.944
I'm guessing

12:16.027 --> 12:18.864
I'll need at least five million won
for a deposit and rent

12:18.947 --> 12:20.615
to get a place of my own.

12:23.702 --> 12:24.578
Right.

12:28.707 --> 12:31.084
CLOUD YOUTH SHELTER

12:37.007 --> 12:38.341
Thank you.

12:39.134 --> 12:39.968
Yeah.

12:41.678 --> 12:42.679
Get home safe.

12:43.472 --> 12:45.432
Sure. See you at school.

13:00.197 --> 13:01.031
Let's go.

13:01.656 --> 13:02.574
Okay.

13:04.951 --> 13:06.411
Ji-a was worried

13:06.495 --> 13:09.164
those guys would come to the shelter
and cause trouble,

13:09.247 --> 13:10.916
and that's why she didn't report them.

13:13.168 --> 13:14.294
In case she'd get kicked out.

13:16.213 --> 13:19.341
I never thought you'd come all this way
looking for her.

13:20.217 --> 13:23.345
The other teachers don't even care
if she comes to school or not.

13:25.514 --> 13:28.350
I doubt you came all this way
to avoid some demerits.

13:28.433 --> 13:30.018
You're here because you were worried.

13:34.189 --> 13:35.273
I'm proud of you.

13:41.279 --> 13:43.657
Mr. Ga, if you go to the US,

13:44.282 --> 13:48.036
will you be doing the work you want to?

13:50.330 --> 13:51.581
It's just…

13:52.457 --> 13:54.543
Just like I love writing novels,

13:54.626 --> 13:56.211
you might have something you like.

13:57.587 --> 14:02.759
Something you like so much
that you can't bear not doing it.

14:02.842 --> 14:04.844
I wondered if that was why you were going.

14:08.557 --> 14:10.600
Perhaps I do have that kind of passion.

14:11.726 --> 14:14.229
But regardless of that,
my number one priority now

14:15.063 --> 14:17.649
is to teach, take care of,

14:18.441 --> 14:19.776
and watch you guys grow.

14:21.945 --> 14:23.196
Nothing else matters.

15:27.177 --> 15:30.972
CHAPTER 35:
WE'LL HELP LIKE YOU'RE FAMILY

15:44.486 --> 15:45.820
Hello, what's up?

15:45.904 --> 15:47.072
-Hey, Jenny!
-Jenny!

15:47.155 --> 15:47.989
I'm back.

15:48.073 --> 15:49.157
-What?
-What are those?

15:49.240 --> 15:51.660
It's a present for you guys.

15:51.743 --> 15:52.952
-Welcome back.
-Enjoy.

15:53.036 --> 15:54.996
-Jenny, I really missed you.
-Hi, Jenny.

16:00.001 --> 16:00.960
I bought these cookies

16:01.044 --> 16:04.464
after waiting in line
for an hour and a half in Yeonnam-dong.

16:04.547 --> 16:06.132
-Thanks.
-Jenny got us these.

16:07.258 --> 16:08.218
Thanks.

16:12.514 --> 16:13.390
Thanks.

16:18.812 --> 16:19.688
What is this?

16:19.771 --> 16:20.939
They're so freaking good.

16:21.022 --> 16:22.607
-Right?
-Yeah.

16:22.691 --> 16:24.401
Jenny, you posted so many stories.

16:24.484 --> 16:25.902
The updates wouldn't stop.

16:25.985 --> 16:28.321
Yeah, you visited so many places.

16:28.405 --> 16:30.782
I went out early
and stayed out until late at night.

16:30.865 --> 16:33.118
My feet hurt so much.

16:33.201 --> 16:34.744
I even got blisters.

16:34.828 --> 16:35.662
Wanna see?

16:35.745 --> 16:37.914
-No, thanks.
-Why would we?

16:37.997 --> 16:39.874
There's really no need.

16:39.958 --> 16:41.084
Your loss.

16:42.585 --> 16:45.004
Come join us, Go-ya.

16:45.088 --> 16:46.631
I'm fine.

16:47.882 --> 16:49.300
-What's up?
-Jenny.

16:49.384 --> 16:50.301
What?

16:50.885 --> 16:53.054
-She doesn't want to?
-Jenny.

16:53.138 --> 16:55.098
-You know our group chat?
-Yeah.

16:55.181 --> 16:57.392
Can you share the list of places
you visited in Seoul?

16:57.475 --> 16:59.519
-Yes, please.
-The Han River and…

16:59.602 --> 17:00.687
Of course.

17:01.855 --> 17:04.774
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

17:06.317 --> 17:07.193
Mr. Ga!

17:07.277 --> 17:09.612
I'm back from Seoul.

17:10.363 --> 17:11.489
How was it?

17:11.573 --> 17:13.408
So much fun.

17:14.242 --> 17:15.285
Sir.

17:16.661 --> 17:18.872
Submit your field trip report
by the end of this week.

17:19.622 --> 17:20.457
Yes, sir.

17:27.505 --> 17:28.882
Time for roll call.

17:28.965 --> 17:29.924
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

17:35.472 --> 17:37.640
Okay, watch carefully.

17:38.558 --> 17:39.893
Keep your feet shoulder-width apart.

17:40.518 --> 17:41.936
Then, bend your knees slightly.

17:42.854 --> 17:44.230
Use your weaker hand for support.

17:44.898 --> 17:45.857
Just place it like this.

17:46.357 --> 17:47.233
And if you just shoot…

17:48.568 --> 17:49.652
it won't go in.

17:51.362 --> 17:52.947
You see that rectangle up there?

17:53.031 --> 17:55.200
If you aim for that when you shoot…

18:00.830 --> 18:02.749
You're the best!

18:02.832 --> 18:03.708
Then, it'll go in.

18:05.418 --> 18:06.252
Now you try.

18:07.295 --> 18:08.129
Ha-su.

18:16.387 --> 18:17.222
There you go.

18:31.694 --> 18:32.737
Come on, you.

18:33.780 --> 18:34.614
Go-ya.

18:36.449 --> 18:37.408
No fooling around.

18:41.287 --> 18:42.413
Hold on.

18:42.497 --> 18:44.082
You have to use one hand. Just one.

18:44.833 --> 18:45.708
One hand, like this.

18:46.501 --> 18:50.463
Her right wrist is not in great shape.

18:51.506 --> 18:53.383
It gets sprained pretty easily.

18:55.093 --> 18:55.927
Really?

18:58.972 --> 19:00.348
It's fine. I can do it.

19:10.400 --> 19:12.193
It's okay to sit this one out.

19:13.236 --> 19:15.154
Did something happen between you two?

19:16.447 --> 19:18.408
No. Why?

19:19.242 --> 19:21.202
The whole vibe is different from usual.

19:22.203 --> 19:23.246
You guys are not smiling.

19:24.289 --> 19:25.123
It's just…

19:25.915 --> 19:28.084
I guess we're feeling
a bit under the weather today.

19:34.048 --> 19:36.259
Something definitely went down.

19:37.260 --> 19:39.721
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

19:50.648 --> 19:52.942
What? Ji-a?

20:07.874 --> 20:10.293
Amazing. Turns out Ji-a's rich.

20:10.376 --> 20:12.921
People that look like her staff
came in a car to pick her up.

20:15.506 --> 20:17.759
Incredible.

20:17.842 --> 20:18.885
I can't believe it!

20:29.771 --> 20:32.148
Sir! What are we going to do? It's Ji-a.

20:32.231 --> 20:34.025
I think those guys from yesterday
grabbed her.

20:34.108 --> 20:35.443
-What do you mean?
-Look at this.

20:35.526 --> 20:37.904
Jenny saw two guys
getting her into a car and driving off.

20:37.987 --> 20:38.821
This is their car.

20:38.905 --> 20:39.948
What do we do?

20:40.031 --> 20:41.616
-You wait here. I'll go find her.
-Okay.

20:42.909 --> 20:45.036
Send me the photos of the car
and their business card.

20:45.119 --> 20:46.412
Yes, sir.

20:50.583 --> 20:51.584
What do I do next?

20:52.210 --> 20:54.587
What else can I do? Think.

20:55.546 --> 20:57.757
Oh, Mr. Jung.

20:58.424 --> 21:00.301
GOOD CONSCIENCE PAYDAY LOANS

21:12.855 --> 21:13.690
Have you chosen?

21:13.773 --> 21:15.108
WE'LL HELP LIKE YOU'RE FAMILY

21:15.191 --> 21:16.818
If you do option C three times,

21:16.901 --> 21:19.320
that's a million won, okay?

21:19.404 --> 21:20.238
Ji-a.

21:21.864 --> 21:23.658
-Sir!
-Sit back down.

21:25.451 --> 21:27.036
Damn.

21:28.371 --> 21:30.039
I told you
I never wanted to see you again.

21:30.540 --> 21:32.333
Have you come all this way?

21:34.335 --> 21:35.503
Who's that?

21:37.463 --> 21:39.090
He's her homeroom teacher.

21:40.758 --> 21:42.010
Goodness me.

21:42.719 --> 21:44.429
So true teachers do keep on giving.

21:47.265 --> 21:49.308
We're really sorry.

21:49.392 --> 21:51.936
The thing is,
when we did the final calculations,

21:52.562 --> 21:54.355
the numbers didn't add up.

21:55.314 --> 21:56.941
What with inflation,

21:57.025 --> 21:58.401
and the way we calculate interest

21:59.444 --> 22:01.529
-having changed and all.
-Exactly.

22:02.113 --> 22:03.990
Interest used to be 20% per month,

22:04.073 --> 22:06.284
but we recently changed to a weekly basis.

22:07.160 --> 22:09.620
During those few weeks
when Ji-a couldn't pay us back,

22:09.704 --> 22:12.373
the interest skyrocketed.

22:15.626 --> 22:18.463
So she still owes us
about two and a half million won.

22:18.546 --> 22:20.048
It was paid in full the other day.

22:20.131 --> 22:22.467
Sir, don't listen to them.

22:22.550 --> 22:23.718
Shut up, you!

22:24.302 --> 22:25.219
Don't move.

22:25.303 --> 22:26.429
Anyhow, sir,

22:27.055 --> 22:29.307
if Ji-a can't pay the money back,

22:29.390 --> 22:31.809
she'll have to go out to work

22:31.893 --> 22:34.020
at the kind of place
where pretty girls work.

22:34.645 --> 22:36.981
Sir, don't give them any more money.

22:37.065 --> 22:38.941
I'll be fine. Just hurry up and leave.

22:43.362 --> 22:44.322
Is there a contract?

22:45.990 --> 22:47.658
Let's see the contract with those terms

22:47.742 --> 22:49.660
drawn up on the day of the loan
if you have it.

22:51.329 --> 22:52.413
Huh?

22:53.247 --> 22:55.166
If you don't have it,
what's your basis for collecting?

23:00.463 --> 23:02.381
You're really starting
to get on my nerves.

23:03.966 --> 23:05.885
You think this is your home turf?

23:07.637 --> 23:09.097
Sir!

23:12.558 --> 23:14.560
What's wrong with you? Huh?

23:17.146 --> 23:19.232
I see you still haven't figured me out.

23:23.820 --> 23:24.654
Oh my!

23:40.711 --> 23:42.338
PAYDAY LOANS

23:48.511 --> 23:49.637
This must be it.

23:50.263 --> 23:52.515
Eui-ju, you stay here.
We'll be right back with them.

23:53.099 --> 23:55.101
-How can I just--
-Stay here.

23:55.184 --> 23:56.185
This won't take long.

24:15.204 --> 24:16.831
Do you love jjajangmyeon that much?

24:16.914 --> 24:17.790
Yes, boss.

24:17.874 --> 24:20.251
Look at you, stuffing your face.

24:20.334 --> 24:21.544
Is it that good?

24:27.383 --> 24:28.467
Mr. Ga!

24:28.551 --> 24:29.677
Are you okay?

24:29.760 --> 24:31.304
Oh, no.

24:31.387 --> 24:32.221
You're okay now.

24:32.305 --> 24:33.556
Oh, I'm sorry.

24:33.639 --> 24:34.724
Oh, no.

24:35.933 --> 24:38.060
Who are these heavenly figures?

24:39.145 --> 24:41.063
What leads you to descend from on high

24:41.147 --> 24:42.815
to visit my humble place?

24:43.399 --> 24:44.358
Was it you bastards

24:45.818 --> 24:46.861
who put him in that state?

24:48.279 --> 24:49.113
That's right.

24:49.697 --> 24:51.032
This is hilarious.

24:51.115 --> 24:52.033
Oh, no…

26:07.566 --> 26:09.568
Subtitle: Paul Carver
